// A raised epoch means ownership was taken over; a missing session means
// the credential was revoked. Either way this instance is permanently
// fenced: it must never mix another byte into the log. The caller proves
// liveness simply by holding the mutex, so the session heartbeat is
// refreshed first (a process blocked waiting for the lock cannot run its
// heartbeat timer) and then never self-fences on staleness.
